{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.DoorVParityNoIdentity","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.DoorVParityNoIdentity","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic"],"declarations":12,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.DoorVParityNoIdentity.twist_clears_only_if_everywhere_alternating","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.DoorVParityNoIdentity.twist_clears_only_if_everywhere_alternating","kind":"theorem","line":201,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/DoorVParityNoIdentity.lean#L201-L212","doc":"**Consequence: the twist clears the obstruction only for a target that\nalternates at *every* consecutive pair.**\n\nIf some pair of the twisted sequence still flips, no non-negative-cone\ncombination can equal it either — so exhibiting the twist does not by itself\nmake the target reachable. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.DoorVParityNoIdentity.obstruction_fires_on_one_of","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.DoorVParityNoIdentity.obstruction_fires_on_one_of","kind":"theorem","line":187,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/DoorVParityNoIdentity.lean#L187-L199","doc":"**The parity twist RELOCATES the obstruction; it cannot remove it.**\n\n`doorV_parity_no_identity` fires as soon as the target has one consecutive sign\nflip. The twist inverts *every* consecutive-pair sign\n(`barTwist_consecutive_product`), so at each `m` where the product is nonzero\nthe obstruction fires on `y` or on its twist — never on neither. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.DoorVParityNoIdentity.barTwist_creates_obstruction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.DoorVParityNoIdentity.barTwist_creates_obstruction","kind":"theorem","line":180,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/DoorVParityNoIdentity.lean#L180-L185","doc":"And it removes it *only* there: if the target had no flip at `m`, the twist\nintroduces one. The twist is therefore exactly the parity, not a weakening. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.DoorVParityNoIdentity.barTwist_removes_obstruction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.DoorVParityNoIdentity.barTwist_removes_obstruction","kind":"theorem","line":168,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/DoorVParityNoIdentity.lean#L168-L178","doc":"**The twist removes exactly the parity obstruction.**\n\n`doorV_parity_no_identity` excludes a non-negative-cone identity precisely when\nthe target has a consecutive sign flip, `y_m · y_{m+1} < 0`. After the twist that\nproduct is strictly positive, so the obstruction does not apply to the twisted\nsequence — and it is removed for *every* `m` at which it fired, with nothing\nelse about the hypothesis changed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.DoorVParityNoIdentity.barTwist_consecutive_product","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.DoorVParityNoIdentity.barTwist_consecutive_product","kind":"theorem","line":160,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/DoorVParityNoIdentity.lean#L160-L166","doc":"**The twist inverts consecutive-pair signs.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.DoorVParityNoIdentity.barTwist_recursion_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.DoorVParityNoIdentity.barTwist_recursion_inv","kind":"theorem","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/DoorVParityNoIdentity.lean#L149-L154","doc":"Conversely: the sign-flipped recurrence twists back to the original. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.DoorVParityNoIdentity.barTwist_recursion","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.DoorVParityNoIdentity.barTwist_recursion","kind":"theorem","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/DoorVParityNoIdentity.lean#L140-L147","doc":"**The twist carries the Stokes carrier's recurrence to a sign-flipped one.**\n`y_{m+2} − (2−q^{m+1})y_{m+1} + y_m = 0` becomes\n`z_{m+2} + (2−q^{m+1})z_{m+1} + z_m = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.DoorVParityNoIdentity.barTwist","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.DoorVParityNoIdentity.barTwist","kind":"def","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/DoorVParityNoIdentity.lean#L137-L138","doc":"The bar-parity twist `z_m = (−1)^m y_m`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.DoorVParityNoIdentity.doorV_parity_no_identity_forall","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.DoorVParityNoIdentity.doorV_parity_no_identity_forall","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/DoorVParityNoIdentity.lean#L98-L108","doc":"Everywhere-alternating specialization: if the GGM target flips sign at\n*every* consecutive pair, no non-negative-cone combination of the\ntensor-square sequences can equal it. Immediate from the pointwise version\nat `m = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.DoorVParityNoIdentity.doorV_parity_no_identity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.DoorVParityNoIdentity.doorV_parity_no_identity","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/DoorVParityNoIdentity.lean#L66-L96","doc":"**Door-v parity NO-IDENTITY (scope-(b) structural exclusion).**\n\nModel of the Door-v situation. `p`, `q` are the non-negative tensor-square\nsequences `f₊²`, `f₋²` (`0 ≤ p n`, `0 ≤ q n`). `y` is the genuinely\nsign-alternating GGM target (`y n · y (n+1) < 0`, i.e. every consecutive\npair flips sign — the `(−1)^m` character). `α, β ≥ 0` are the sign-preserving\ncoefficients the tensor-square positivity forces.\n\nConclusion: NO such `(α, β)` reproduces the target — `α·p + β·q = y` is\nimpossible. Proof: the left side lies in the non-negative positive cone\n(`posCone_nonneg`), so an identity would force `y ≥ 0` everywhere,\ncontradicting a single sign flip (`nonneg_not_signalternating`). One\nconsecutive pair suffices, so genuine alternation *anywhere* already\nexcludes the identity.\n\nThis is a scope-(b) exclusion: the cited invariant is the proved\nnon-negativity of a real square, not a numerical near-match. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:c1-ggm-bar-parity-faces","label":"conj:c1-ggm-bar-parity-faces","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/c1-ggm-bar-parity-faces.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.DoorVParityNoIdentity.posCone_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.DoorVParityNoIdentity.posCone_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/DoorVParityNoIdentity.lean#L56-L64","doc":"A non-negative-coefficient combination of two non-negative sequences is\nitself pointwise non-negative — the positive cone of `{p, q}`. The\ntensor-square realization forces exactly this sign structure (both\ncoefficients act on non-negative squares). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.DoorVParityNoIdentity.nonneg_not_signalternating","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.DoorVParityNoIdentity.nonneg_not_signalternating","kind":"theorem","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/DoorVParityNoIdentity.lean#L47-L54","doc":"**The core parity fact.** A pointwise non-negative real sequence is never\nsign-alternating: for every `n`, the product of consecutive terms is\nnon-negative, so it cannot be `< 0`. This is the exact invariant behind the\nDoor-v residual — the tensor-square solutions `f₊²`, `f₋²` are non-negative\nsquares, hence carry no consecutive sign flip. ","signatureChunk":0}]}